@user1:
We should store this in options instead of hardcoding

@user1:
besides that, not sure this should be handled by us

@author:
1) i don't think its place should be in options, because they are not actually changeable "options" per se for user supposed to change/override, it's hardlimits given by exchange. but ok, i'll move them into options.
2)  this is the only way we can make this work, it is needed in calculations

@author:
that list defines at what distance we switch from "current" to "historical" endpoint. this is how we do on other exchanges too (i.e. okx ...)

@user1:
If you keep it in options and the exchange decides to update those values it's easier to override on the user side

@author:
yes, I had moved them in options already.

