@user1:
this is actually incorrect and should be 
`[self.choices[0][1]] if self.choices else None` for both raw and serialized (its also incorrect in main). Should be this way, similar to Dropdown multiselect, otherwise the code snippets in api docs don't work as expected. 

@author:
Yeah you're right

@user1:
Please instead update the device entries and remove the config entry id from them. If there are no other config entries remaining the device entry will be removed automatically. That's safer than removing the device entry directly as it's (theoretically) possible for multiple config entries (from any integration) to be connected to the same device entry.

Example:
https://github.com/home-assistant/core/blob/7dc9ad63bd0503cc3298f99ae415a2718cb7f40d/homeassistant/components/tradfri/__init__.py#L191-L193

